Chonkstep: Follow VirtIO framebuffer mode changes

Before each frame, ask SFGOP whether the VirtIO framebuffer changed and lay frames out for the new one. The panel output takes the new size at that frame boundary: the scene, then the wl_output preferred and current mode, which replaces the old one in the mode list, the shell chrome and work areas, layer surfaces and pointer bounds, with one full repaint. A size the scene refuses ends the frame with an error. Clients and windows stay.

